#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1115
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "<Account>The account</Account> is the identity: an email and a password. Everything in groups is done by a <Profile>profile</Profile>. One account can have several profiles, say a business, a private and a club one. The code does not tell them apart by purpose, only unique from shared. A shared profile is used by every account that accepts a <ProfileInvitation>profile invitation</ProfileInvitation>."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1219
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "<Tagging>Tagging</Tagging> joins a <Tag>tag</Tag> with exactly one group, profile, event, value or file, and the database checks that. A tag without an owner is public. A tag with an owner is seen only by that profile."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1123
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group> opened from a <Value>value</Value> is a thread. One value has at most one thread, and a thread always inherits members. There is one root, with no parent and no creator. All other groups have both, even direct conversations, which sit right under the root."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1227
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <GroupInvitation>group invitation</GroupInvitation> goes from profile to profile. If the invited account has no profile yet, an <GroupAccountInvitation>account invitation</GroupAccountInvitation> is kept, which becomes an ordinary invitation as soon as the account gets its first profile. A <GroupJoinRequest>join request</GroupJoinRequest> goes the other way. When accepted it is deleted, and an <GroupJoinRequestApproval>approved request</GroupJoinRequestApproval> stays with the name of whoever admitted the member."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:559
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A file attached to a value. The bytes are in storage, and the row keeps what the browser reported about the file."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1155
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group can inherit members: it then holds all the members of its parent and their roles. Those rows in <GroupMembership>memberships</GroupMembership> and <GroupMemberRole>member roles</GroupMemberRole> are marked as inherited and leave with the membership in the parent. Members added in the group itself stay. When a group stops inheriting, the inherited rows become its own and nobody falls out. The exception is an app withdrawing a group: the inherited members then leave and the direct ones stay."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:857
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group contains values, and a value opens a thread, which is a group again. That is why sub-groups and threads share one model. The arrows read as sentences, from subject to object. These are the main entities, and all of them are under All tables."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:697
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group public from the root must be public."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1193
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group's description can be an app"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:927
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A group's description does not have to be text. The default description and every <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription> can be an app: a program written by members who may edit the group, which runs on the group's page, in a frame of its own, for everyone who opens it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:502
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A join table: which account may use which profile. A unique profile allows only one account. The code checks that, the database does not know about it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:915
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A key over two columns holds both rows in the same group. The schema in the code does not show that."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:678
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A lasting record of who admitted whom to a group and when. It is created in the same transaction that deletes the request and creates the membership."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:601
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member's answer for one occurrence, named by its local start date. Whoever declined gets no reminders for that occurrence."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:629
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A member's own reminders for every occurrence, in place of the organizer's. An empty list turns them off, and without a row the member gets the event's reminders."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:463
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A person's identity: the email and password they log in with. It takes no part in groups, where a profile acts. An account remembers which profile it is using now, which profile gets the invitations sent to the account, and which profile invited it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:671
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile asks to join a group. An accepted request is deleted, and an approval stays in its place."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:650
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile invites another profile to a group. Accepting it creates the membership."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:531
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A profile is a member of a group. An inherited membership exists only through the parent group and leaves with the membership there."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:538
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A role given to a member in one group. In the database it points at the membership, so it cannot exist without one, although the schema in the code says it points at a profile. The role is kept as text, by its key, as it can come from an ancestor's manifest. `everyone` is never written here."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:523
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A role of a manifest. For each of the %{count} permissions it says allowed, denied or nothing, and a denial wins. The built-in ones are `admin`, which has everything, and `everyone`, which every member has."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:636
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A tag without an owner is public and part of one vocabulary for the whole app. A tag with an owner is private and only that profile sees it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:484
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A technical table with no links to the rest of the domain: the `OAuth` refresh token the app uses to send email through `Gmail`."
msgstr ""

