#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1139
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Poll>poll</Poll> names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that vote, that see the results and that see the details, and the organizer and those who manage polls always see them. Once a <PollBallot>ballot</PollBallot> is in, what voters saw no longer changes, except the deadline. One account gives one vote, whichever of its profiles it uses, and a profile several accounts share votes on its own. A secret poll keeps no answers on its ballots, only the count of each <PollOption>answer</PollOption> grows, so neither the group's admins nor an app can see who voted for what. No counts show before its end, and a finished one is not opened again. A public poll also takes the votes of signed-in non-members of a public group. Deleting the <Value>value</Value> that carries a poll deletes the poll."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1163
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new <Group>group</Group> can start from a preset: chat, folder, announcements, feed, polls, form, map or page. A preset sets what any group can have, so all of it can be changed later. The group keeps only the preset's name: its avatar shows that kind while the group still fits it, and the list of sub-groups can be narrowed to one kind. Announcements also get a <GroupManifest>manifest</GroupManifest> of their own, in which `everyone` no longer writes. A feed is two groups, one with the Feed app and one below it with FeedCreator, and each keeps its own copy of its app, so a new version reaches only the feeds made after it. A group for polls, a form and a map keep a copy of their app the same way, and a form gets its two groups for files only once it needs them. The root offers no map, as it has one of its own."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:951
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A new value reaches right away, with no refresh, everyone who has the app open and may see it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:969
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app can keep its <Value>values</Value> under rules its editors set: which <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> write and which read everything, one answer per person, changing one's own answer, a deadline, anonymous answers and, in a public group, answers from signed-in non-members. Potok also scores a quiz by a key only the editors see, counts the answers for a summary, keeps the files sent with them in two sub-groups of the app's group, and sends a push about each new answer to whoever asks for it. That is how a group becomes a form."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1201
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's data carry their own rules"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1203
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "An app's settings are one <Value>value</Value> of its own: the app's data, a secret part only its editors read, and the rules of its other collections, which Potok holds to on every call. A rule names the <GroupRole>roles</GroupRole> that write and those that read everything; everyone else reads only what they wrote, and those who may edit the group always read all. A collection without a rule is closed the same way. One answer per person counts one account once, as a poll does. An answer written while its collection was anonymous never shows its author to anyone but the author, though its time shows, and whoever rewrites the app's code could still get around it. Files sent with answers are values with a <ValueAttachment>file</ValueAttachment> in two sub-groups of the app's group: a closed one, whose members alone open them, and one that inherits the members. Whoever sent a file can always open it."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:967
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Collects answers by its own rules"
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:942
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Each app has its own <Value>values</Value>, apart from the other apps of the group. It can search them, sort them, count them, add them up and read them page by page, the newest first if it likes."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:960
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "It can also read the values of the group's other apps, except those kept under rules, and it writes only to its own."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1072
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Members read and save values, and so do signed-in non-members where an app's rules open that to them in a public group. Rules can narrow it further, and the number of saves is limited."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:766
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Only app data has a collection, named with small letters, digits, - and _."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1076
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Potok checks who answers, when, how many times and how much, not what an answer says."
msgstr ""

#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1195
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "The default description and every <GroupAltDescription>alternative description</GroupAltDescription> can be an app. Its data are <Value>values</Value> marked as data, and each of them knows which app it belongs to and which of the app's collections holds it. A composite key holds them in the same group, and deleting an alternative description deletes its data too."
msgstr ""

