#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1179
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group>'s place can be an area instead of a point, as a local community covers its streets: a border drawn on the map or brought from a GeoJSON file, set by whoever may edit the group. The area keeps a pin, which the server puts inside it by itself. An area holds a group when it holds that group's pin, so every place shows the areas around it, smallest first, and an area inside a bigger one lies in it too. Each viewer sees only the areas of the groups they see. On the root's map an area is only the shape of its group: the filters keep it or leave it out like any group, and once it is wide enough it also shows its border, under the pins; a tap on the map lists the areas there, and a filter keeps only the groups inside chosen areas, which stay outlined."
