#: lib/potok_ide_web/domain_copy.ex:1187
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "A <Group>group</Group>'s place can also be a route, as a walk, a race, a march or a bike path runs: a line drawn on the map or brought from a GPX, KML or GeoJSON file, set by whoever may edit the group. A place is a point, an area or a route, never an area and a route at once. The route keeps its pin at its start, where people meet, which the server puts there by itself, and the map marks its end with a ring. A route lies in every area it passes through, not only in the one it starts in, so its page lists those areas and the filter by area keeps it. On the root's map a route is only the shape of its group, as an area is: the filters keep it or leave it out, and once it is wide enough its line is drawn over the areas, under the pins, in a layer of its own; a tap on the line opens the group, and a link to the map can show one route, whatever the filters."
